elt-a55eae3a76.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bend-eb0c045684.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/eight-6babcf3acd.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/man-73c2d6b358.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/meat-cb2e88bc60.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/milk-c17e4dae82.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/pet-d3fdb9c585.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/seal-72c51151e1.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/smile-aa48df9359.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/feather-300d9c89bc.mp3","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/top.webp","The concrete target picture supports an exact required spoken word. None of the printed spelling alternatives is narrated.","bed gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","clean","complete_heard_blend_spelling","drop","empty","have","like","made","mock-foundation-word:bug","mock-foundation-word:flap","mock-foundation-word:fog","mock-foundation-word:pond","mock-foundation-word:rug","original_mock_depth","src/data/literacyMockFoundationBlendCapacity.js","stone","tired","white","with","writing_revision","yes",21,30,"/audio/phonemes/d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bank-55756b28b8.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/best-e477070e8d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/big-77dcc4f0f8.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/carrot-11102bebd6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/chain-31d77480b3.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/did-3574c3a4a7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/dock-e748cc0114.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/drive-70ccbe7b61.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/egg-1ea56c84db.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/get-b60d152236.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/hot-9d7d07d2d8.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/jug-896f77295e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/nap-98714bbe19.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/nine-200651a3c9.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/not-601ecd1646.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/out-3b23d71f90.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/potato-70de00fca7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/rib-946cfc9695.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/ride-bfdbf56047.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/shout-2084ada19d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/stop-5052fe0221.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/zip-adf43ee65e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/rip-6bb9b91f11.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/spill-95390f4d8d.mp3","/images/assessment/generated/concepts/sing.webp","/images/assessment/generated/concepts/write.webp","/images/assessment/generated/sequencing/child-drinks-water.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-swim.webp","/images/assessment/long-vowels/moon.webp","/images/assessment/release-support/targets/rip-ab8e59.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/eep/sleep-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/ick/kick-02.webp","/images/child-mode/short-a/ram.webp","/media/rhyming/images/tag.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/can.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/den.webp","A model castle filled the classroom doorway. People bumped it when they entered. The builders moved it onto a side table, and people could walk through without touching it.","AY","After using the magnifier, Sol left it in his coat. The nature group searched the shelf and could not start. Sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","Ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. She showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. The book returned to the shelf.","Bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. She carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. The whole set reached the hall together.","Dad","Directions and a required reference word, where the existing task supplies one, are spoken. Printed word alternatives remain silent.","Distinguish a related background detail from evidence that serves the paragraph’s specific purpose.","Eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. At rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. He liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","Hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. A helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. Hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","Identify the medial vowel while retaining the additional phonemes of an initial or final consonant cluster.","Isolate the first single phoneme of a two-consonant spoken onset while rejecting the immediately following cluster member and a close voiced/unvoiced alternative.","Ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. His friend began looking for a loose window. Ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","Jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. They nearly bumped. Jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","Lea took a ruler from Ben’s desk because he was outside. Ben returned and could not finish his chart. Next time Lea asked first, and Ben found a spare ruler for her.","Leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. Dad asked her to touch the soil. It was already wet. They moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","Lou","Mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. She looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. She put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","Milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. She had no chance to try a piece. He showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","Noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. The teacher fed them. The next day Noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","Oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. His group had none left. He returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","Order words or distinguish a complete simple thought from fragments.","Picture for hen","Picture for rat","Ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. He asked a helper to carry the other end. Together they moved it onto the trolley.","Separate complete sentences using full stops, question marks and exclamation marks.","The exact existing spoken word supplies the phonological stimulus; the reviewed target picture retains entry access. The response is one sound-mapping letter, never the whole blend.","The group began a game without explaining it to a new child. She ran to the wrong end and stopped. They showed her the goal and played a slow round together before starting again.","The group decorated a cart while its loose wheel still wobbled. The cart could not carry their bags. They fixed the wheel first on the next cart, then added ribbons when it rolled properly.","The stimulus is three atomic phoneme recordings. Only replayable spoken alternatives supply the responses; no print or target-word recording is exposed.","Tom told a visitor that the hall was “over there.” The visitor chose the wrong door. Tom named the blue door beside the stairs, and the visitor found the hall.","Two builders pulled their cardboard bridge towards different tables. A joint came loose. They stopped, chose one place together and carried the bridge there side by side.","Two runners began from different lines. The nearer runner won, but nobody knew who was faster. They started again from one line and could compare their running.","Una coloured the blank part of her friend’s drawing to help. Her friend had wanted to leave it white for snow. On the next drawing Una asked what was needed and held the paper instead.","When Kim lost, she pushed the board and scattered the pieces. Her friend stopped playing. Kim helped set it up again and asked for another game without changing the old result.","Which letters complete the word?","a bridge over water","a handle for carrying a jar","a hinged lid on a toy","a point scored in a game","a tree’s leafy branch","a tree’s longest root","ban","break","bucket","button","candle","cat gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","complete_short_vowel_spelling:short_a","construct_sentence","crane","cup does not match the supplied spoken_medial_vowel_discrimination evidence.","dry","flip","hide","hip","literacy.print_concepts.two-sentences","map_spoken_word_to_digraph_spelling","mock-foundation-word:sun","off","phonemeCueKeys","pronoun_reference","rim","short_a","side","span","src/data/literacyMockFoundationReadingCapacity.js","src/data/literacyMockWritingOrganizationCapacity.js","step","sun gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","take","tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/digraphs.mjs","tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/r_controlled_vowels.mjs","trap","trip","tunnel","/audio/phonemes/m.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/instruction/inside-the-oven-0b7f122918.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/above-the-hall-entrance-f0e0fca4ea.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/along-the-path-95bac810bf.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/beneath-the-walkway-699a8394be.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bud-e48e211ff1.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/checking-the-clock-614cf31065.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/choosing-a-seat-3773a23b17.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/clapping-for-lou-30d56e6e0b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/closing-a-basket-cbf8f7d5fe.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/closing-a-book-25dd9a5407.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/counting-the-bags-09b5516800.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/countin