S/isolated_word/picking-a-flower-9fc2bf2545.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/pop-2c1d45eaaf.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/putting-on-a-hat-60257b5476.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/quietly-72e50d19a6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/rag-c42b54ef88.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/record-useful-details-before-they-are-easy-to-forget-e7335afc21.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sat-9f3e1919d7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/singing-a-song-291824bf6b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sum-dbf810b510.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/switching-on-a-lamp-7984df5ab2.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/taking-a-photo-abd7ea4140.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/taking-off-her-gloves-1c38fa5293.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tie-18c0eb5de2.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tying-a-rope-f4b84ecf65.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/unfolding-a-blanket-b885226d55.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-specific-feedback-to-improve-unclear-work-4066dd1a3a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/washing-a-brush-99c42792ad.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/waving-to-gran-167b8466df.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/window-ccf2fb3748.mp3","/images/assessment/blends/clap.webp","/images/assessment/digraphs/shell.webp","/images/assessment/generated/concepts/jump.webp","/images/assessment/generated/concepts/trunk.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/deer.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/seal.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/tie.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/drink-d876a37b.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/mud-4f3d05c0.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/zoo.webp","A bed","A bug","A complete sentence starts with a capital letter; a capital later in the sentence cannot replace it.","A full oral task; not a printed spelling or word-reading item.","A mug","A","Ada hung the picture list above her own head. The younger children could not see what to collect. She crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","Alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. The paint dried while she searched. Before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","Asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. Her friend kept waiting under the tree. Asha went back and explained the change. Her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","Ben","Bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. He put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. Bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office.","Ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. A different wheel stuck when he pushed it. He turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again.","Extract the first phoneme from the correct choice’s consonant cluster rather than match its second cluster member or a voiced/unvoiced near sound.","Finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. The wet joint slid apart. He glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. This time the handle stayed on.","Gran","Insect. Listen to the first sound. Which word has the same vowel sound?","Jo kept the game scores in her head. After a break she could not remember which team had seven points. On the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. The teams could check the score after the break.","Listen. Build the missing word.","Listen. Pick the missing word.","Listen. Which printed word matches the recording?","Maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. The puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. She replaced the tray. After the next watering, the shelf stayed dry.","Olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. The copied pattern was different. Olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. Her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","Omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. When the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. For his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","Picture for leg","Picture for mop","Picture for net","Picture for pig","Picture for pin","Poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. She chose the wrong longer strip. She laid them flat with their left ends together. Now she could see which strip reached farther.","Recognize sentence-initial capitalisation in one complete simple thought; no sentence repair or paragraph judgment is required.","Tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. He could not remember which ones he had checked. He placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. He found the stamp in a new drawer.","Tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. Their leaves overlapped and bent. She moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. The leaves no longer pressed against one another.","The capital identifies the proper name even within a longer sentence.","The existing exact anchor instruction and target recording are unchanged; every new hidden-label answer card has its reviewed picture and exact word recording.","The sentence starts with a capital; names and I keep their capitals, while ordinary nouns inside the sentence do not take extra capitals.","Y","Zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. The cardboard began to bend. She stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap.","apple does not match the supplied familiar_word_across_categories evidence.","bid","birds","close","cold","contextual_high_frequency_word_encoding","contextual_high_frequency_word_recognition","deep","fed","hfw-wo