.","A quick guess is enough when things look familiar.","A roof directs rain into a storage tank.","A screen catches leaves before the tank.","A small job is never useful to the whole group.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","A star was needed for a box to be sent, but not every starred box went.","A stronger push is the best way to solve every problem.","A thing is free to use whenever its owner is away.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Add more water before checking the soil in a pot.","Adding more decoration always makes a model work better.","Affix meaning is interpreted from the complete orally accessible scenario and choices; independent passage reading is not a difficulty condition.","Agree on a plan before working together. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Agree on a plan before working together. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Apples were in all the baskets; pears were in just one.","Ask a visitor to try each door in turn.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Ask people to step over a model in a doorway.","Ask walkers which direction they want to go.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Bees carry pollen between different flowering plants.","Bees collect nectar to take to their hive.","Begin the next round before a newcomer understands the goal.","Being first matters more than waiting for other people.","Bo put the brushes away before washing them.","Bo washed the brushes while they remained in the cupboard.","Boxes without stars were the only ones sent.","Build a taller castle so visitors can see it.","Change the old result before asking to play again.","Check player names before announcing a score.","Check soil when deciding how much to water.","Check that string fits before tying a booklet.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Choose a different activity when a tool is missing.","Choose a different model when a piece does not fit.","Choose a faster game when a newcomer runs the wrong way.","Choose a longer game before doing a classroom job.","Choose a longer route to practise carrying a heavy crate.","Choose a longer slide when the playground is busy.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Choose a wider block to push through the gap.","Choose another book while someone else repairs the first.","Choose brighter decorations when a cart will not roll.","Choose only jobs you have done before.","Choose the quickest watering plan for every pot.","Choose your favourite colours for another person’s drawing.","Choose your favourite materials before the others arrive.","Cleaning wet paint quickly can save a model.","Collecting rain provides water for dry days.","Compare runners by looking at the colour of their shoes.","Complete one person’s crown before giving others materials.","Composting reuses scraps to improve garden soil.","Construct at least six spoken phonemes across meaningful compound parts or a morpheme extension, preserving vowel teams and rejecting spare graphemes.","Construct five spoken phonemes, preserving a vowel team and rejecting two spare graphemes.","Construct six or more spoken phonemes across a meaningful compound or morpheme extension, retaining vowel-team spellings and rejecting two spare graphemes.","Cut the next piece quickly before checking its length.","D-SEMANTIC","D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","Dad put out the candles before the song ended.","Damage stops mattering when somebody puts it out of sight.","Decide on your own before the plan is finished.","Different starting points make every race equally fair.","Draw more decorations before asking a reader.","Each item orders the same three supplied prerequisite events along one causal chain. Extra description does not change that ordering operation.","Empty spaces in someone’s work should always be filled in.","Every round and square button was used.","Every round button was used, and every square button was left unused.","Every starred box was sent to the hall.","Every used button was square.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Feather layers keep swimming ducks warm and dry.","Fill a blank space before the artist notices it.","Fill a cart with bags before repairing its loose wheel.","Finish a learner’s puzzle whenever they pause.","Finish each fold as quickly as you can.","Finish the whole sign before testing the paint.","Finish your work quickly before returning a borrowed ruler.","Flower visits feed bees and help plants.","Gardeners gather plant scraps into a heap.","Give each runner a different starting place.","Give every plant the same amount of water.","Give specific details when another person needs to find something. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Give specific details when another person needs to find something. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Give useful guidance while leaving another person a chance to try. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Give useful guidance while leaving another person a chance to try. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Helping means doing every hard step for the learner.","Hide a tear so you can finish the bird.","Hold five spoken phonemes, retain a vowel team and reject two spare graphemes.","Hooks carry some seeds on animal fur.","How a bus stop helps people plan and wait. It combines both evidence parts.","How a bus stop helps people plan and wait.","How a helper repairs clothes before the next show.","How a roof keeps the waiting seats dry.","How afternoon helpers read the earlier care chart.","How an arrival board helps people plan their journey.","How backpack parts help us sort and carry things. It combines both evidence parts.","How backpack parts help us sort and carry things.","How costumes are organised and kept ready to wear. It combines both evidence parts.","How costumes are organised and kept ready to wear.","How helpers supply animals and pass on care records. It combines both evidence parts.","How helpers supply animals and pass on care records.","How measuring ingredients prepares bowls before cooking.","How morning helpers refill food and water bowls.","How named rails help actors find their own costumes.","How shoulder straps spread the weight of a backpack.","How small pockets keep pencils away from books.","How the class prepares for cooking and clears afterwards. It combines both evidence parts.","How the class prepares for cooking and clears afterwards.","How volunteers collect books that families have finished.","How volunteers gather books and help visitors choose. It combines both evidence parts.","How volunteers gather books and help visitors choose.","How volunteers help visitors find books they may enjoy.","How washing tools leaves the kitchen ready afterwards.","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again.","J","Judge a plant’s soil only by looking at its leaves.","Judge what a bag holds by the pictures outside.","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle.","Keep a problem secret while you finish the job.","Keep drainage holes clear when caring for plants.","Keep pot information only in your memory.","Keep the difficult pieces so a learner cannot choose them.","Keep the first plan even when it does not work.","Keep the same marks after a reader gets confused.","Keep the whole load when a crate is difficult to lift.","Keep trying to lift the largest part by yourself.","Keep useful tools with you for the next activity.","Keep using the first fix until it works.","Large eyes help owls see in dim light.","Learning a stitch can help mend a costume.","Leave a feeding job for the person who notices it.","Leave a tap dripping for the next person’s bowl.","Leave shared spaces clear for the people who need them. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Leave shared spaces clear for the people who need them. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Light and position change a toy’s shadow.","Light wings carry some seeds on wind.","Locate one misused homophone in a short concrete sentence; there is no correctly used instance of the same spelling competing with it.","Locate one misused homophone while retaining another correct occurrence of exactly the same printed word. Its meaning and grammatical role, rather than spotting the spelling, determine which token needs changing.","Look carefully beneath a stopped toy car to find what is blocking its wheels.","Look for another cause before telling anyone about a spill.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Make every paper fold carefully to avoid tearing a wing on the bird.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Measuring string can help a model fit.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again.","Move the bridge quickly before choosing its destination.","Moving a toy nearer makes larger shadows.","Moving faster always makes the work more accurate.","Moving the torch sideways shifts the shadow.","Mum","New players should learn the rules by guessing alone.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon.","Noor","Offer backstage jobs to children who prefer them.","Oiled outer feathers help swimming ducks stay dry.","Omits the required initial capital for sentence_capital.","One person should keep the best supplies for their own work.","Only one basket contained any fruit.","Only try a job after knowing that you will enjoy it.","Pears were in all the baskets; apples were in just one.","Picture for hat","Picture for pen","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Pond plants give adult frogs hiding places.","Pond water holds frog eggs and young.","Ponds meet frogs’ needs through their lives.","Printed case is the evidence. The choices have identical wording and punctuation; speaking them or adding an object picture would not establish capitalization.","Pull harder when a partner chooses another direction.","Put a damaged book back before anyone sees the tear.","Put the cards away before anyone can check them.","Put the pieces away when another player wins.","Put the sentences in order.","Puts a capital inside the word instead of using its conventional initial capital.","Quietly hiding a mistake is the best way to fix it.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat.","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them.","Read or supply the medial short vowel in a three-phoneme word. A consonant digraph or doubled letter does not add a phoneme.","Recycle a closed bag before sorting the puppet clothes.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily.","Repeat the first step when the plan changes.","Repeat the same movement with more force.","Repeat the same pointing words from farther away.","Repeating the same vague words always makes directions clear.","Return shared things to the place where others expect them. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Return shared things to the place where others expect them. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Roots collect water from the surrounding soil.","Roots hold plants firmly in the ground.","Roots support plants and supply their needs.","Seeds reach new places in several ways.","Select the conventional r-controlled spelling against alternatives with a different vowel; extra consonants alone do not establish a harder tier.","Several body features help owls hunt at night.","Share what is available so everyone can take part. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Share what is available so everyone can take part. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Shared tools should stay with the last person who used them.","Slide more quickly when someone is still at the bottom.","Small living things break plant scraps down.","Soft feather edges make flying owls quiet.","Soft inner feathers keep swimming ducks warm.","Start a new model before asking for help.","Start the sentence with one capital letter. These other words use small letters.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Taking the biggest job alone always helps the group most.","Testing is only useful after all the work is done.","The best place to build is wherever there is empty floor.","The brushes were already washed when Bo put them away.","The candles were out before the song began.","The existing exact ending instruction/recording and response choices are retained, with an existing reviewed exact-target picture matching the entry access condition.","The first part of a message is all you need.","The first sign of a problem always tells you its cause.","The last clap came after both movements.","The last clap came before both movements.","The last clap came between standing up and sitting down.","The next person should deal with supplies left running.","The small puppy.","The song had already ended when Dad put out the candles.","The stronger partner should choose the plan for everyone.","The supplied single relevant relation supports “five”.","The supplied single relevant relation supports “four”.","The supplied single relevant relation supports “three”.","The supplied single relevant relation supports “two”.","This detail supports the specific topic announced by the opening sentence.","This names a related thing in the scene, rather than the meaning of chest at the named occurrence.","This names a related thing in the scene, rather than the meaning of clip at the named occurrence.","This names a related thing in the scene, rather than the meaning of coach at the named occurrence.","Trust your first guess when the job seems easy.","Try a small amount of paint on a scrap before painting a whole sign.","Try an unfamiliar role before deciding it is not for you. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Try an unfamiliar role before deciding it is not for you. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Turn a wide object carefully so it can pass through a narrow gap.","Under the chair.","Use a bigger bowl instead of closing a dripping tap.","Use a complete plan when building a tower.","Use a hand signal when music is too loud.","Use an absent person’s things while their seat is empty.","Use more force when an object stops moving.","Use one plan for everything, even when needs differ.","Use the first paint because it is familiar.","Use the same care for every unlabelled pot.","Use the same conditions when making a fair comparison. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Use the same conditions when making a fair comparison. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Wait beside a heavy box until every job is finished.","Wait for a clear turn when people share an activity. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Wait for a clear turn when people share an activity. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Wait until the play ends before trying a scenery job.","Which word names an animal?","Work alone so nobody needs to hear your problem.","Worm tunnels let air enter the soil.","Worms change soil by tunnelling and feeding.","Worms pull fallen leaves beneath the ground.","Writing a complete list can help you remember everything to pack.","a bee visits flowers for nectar to take to its hive. pollen sticks to its body during these visits. some pollen reaches another flower when the bee lands there, helping that plant make seeds while the bee collects its food.","a board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due. people use it to decide whether to wait or walk. a roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","a clear material for windows","a container for a drink","a duck’s soft inner feathers trap warm air near its body. it spreads oil over its outer feathers, which helps water roll off. these different layers protect the duck when it swims in cold water.","a group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. the cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it. for a birthday, ari spent all his coins on wrapping paper and could not buy the card he needed. next time he chose the card first and used the coins left over for wrapping paper.","a kind of tree","a learner at a school","a line of traffic that cannot move freely","a long-legged bird","a machine for lifting heavy loads","a machine that moves air","a model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. the builders moved it onto a side table. at the reading corner, bags covered every seat. rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","a model castle filled the classroom doorway. people bumped it when they entered. the builders moved it onto a side table, and people could walk through without touching it.","a new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. they showed her and practised a slow round. in class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. a partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","a particular day on a calendar","a person who supports a team","a sweet brown fruit with a stone","a sweet fruit spread for food","a toy blocks light from a torch. moving the torch to one side shifts the shadow to the other side. moving the toy closer to the torch makes its shadow larger. the same toy can make different shadows without changing its own shape.","ada rushed her folds and tore a paper bird. she slowed down at the difficult folds on the next one. malik rushed to announce a game score and read the wrong line. he paused to check the names before announcing the next score.","ada rushed to fold a paper bird and tore a wing. she slowed down at each fold on the next bird, which stayed whole.","adapt","after using the magnifier, sol left it in his coat. the nature group searched the shelf and could not start. sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","all_none","an owl’s large eyes help it see in dim light. its hearing helps it locate small animals it cannot easily see. soft feather edges make its flight quiet as it approaches prey at night.","an upright support for a fence","art","arun moved the screen after naming the puppet. he had opened a bag before naming it.","at book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. they put books with missing pages aside. other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","at the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls. they tick each completed job on a chart. afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. she showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. the book returned to the shelf.","ava tore the cover of a shared book. she helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. he helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","ball names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","banana names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. at a display, ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. he made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. she carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. the whole set reached the hall together.","bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. she had washed a brush before drawing the line.","bea forgot which seeds she had sown. she labelled the next pots so she could care for each plant correctly.","before choosing a book, noor stacked the cushions. she had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. this makes it easy to find each amount when needed. after cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","before packing his notebook, arun tied his scarf. before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","bell names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","bird names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","bo began building before hearing the whole plan. his tower was the wrong shape. he listened to the full plan and rebuilt it correctly.","bo built the wrong shape after hearing only part of a plan. he listened to the full plan before rebuilding. uma guessed where a walker wanted to go and gave wrong directions. she listened to the whole request before answering again.","broom names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","cat does not match the supplied spoken_medial_vowel_discrimination evidence.","cause","cheese names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","clamp","closing the shade happens before filling the trough, which happens before counting the visitors; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","complete_short_vowel_spelling:short_e","complete_short_vowel_spelling:short_o","compound","compoundParts","construct_extended_compound","construct_five_phoneme_team","correctHomophoneTokenIndex","costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name. actors find the clothes for their own role there. a repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","dad counted the cups after closing a basket. he had unfolded a blanket before closing the basket.","dark","dolphin names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it. at music club, may rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. she tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. at rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. he liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","eve painted a whole sign with thin paint that was hard to read. she tested thicker paint on a scrap before painting a new sign.","eve put out the menus after wiping the table. she had moved the vase before wiping the table.","eve’s thin paint made a sign hard to read. she tested thicker paint on a scrap before repainting. lou tied all the pages into a booklet, then found the holes too small. he tested the string through one hole before making the next booklet.","five clean cups were on the tray.","five red pencils were sharpened.","four evening tickets were left for sale.","four story books were on the top shelf.","fox names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","gardeners put leaves and fruit peel in a heap. tiny living things break the scraps down over time. gardeners mix the finished material into soil, returning useful material to the garden instead of throwing all the scraps away.","gently","grapes names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. a helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","hana left a tap dripping, then closed it fully when a helper showed her. at the craft table, bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. he took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","herd gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","herd","here gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","horse names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","identify_read_short_vowel_sound:short_e","identify_read_short_vowel_sound:short_o","ivo blamed the wind after scattering the score cards. his friend looked for a loose window until ivo explained the spill. at a match, mae wrote an extra goal for her team. she told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. his friend began looking for a loose window. ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","jem slid before the child below had moved away, and they nearly bumped. on his next turn he waited for a clear space. at music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. they agreed to play one short turn each.","jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. they nearly bumped. jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","jo gave every plant the same water. one pot stayed soggy. she checked its soil and watered it less, and it grew stronger.","jo watered every plant alike until one stayed soggy. she changed its watering to suit the soil. sal gave everyone the same job in a play; a quiet child struggled to announce scenes. sal offered a backstage job that suited the child better.","kim scattered the board after losing. she helped set it up and asked for another game without changing the result. a runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","kit could not push a wide block through a gap until she turned it sideways. at the pool, ren tried to hear a spoken cue over loud music. he agreed on a hand signal instead, and the group responded together.","kit kept forcing a wide block through a narrow gap. she turned it sideways, and it fitted through.","kit put on a hat after tying a rope. before tying the rope, kit had waved to gran.","kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","lea took a ruler from ben’s desk because he was outside. ben returned and could not finish his chart. next time lea asked first, and ben found a spare ruler for her.","lea took ben’s ruler while he was outside, leaving him unable to finish his chart. next time she asked, and he found her a spare. otter used badger’s umbrella without asking. badger searched for it in the rain. later otter asked to borrow it and agreed when to return it.","leaf gives the vowel a different conventional sound from the requested short vowel.","leila guessed that drooping leaves meant dry soil. touching the wet soil led her to move the plant from the hot sun instead. arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. a notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. he checked the rack and found his hat.","leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. dad asked her to touch the soil. it was already wet. they moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","letters delivered to a home","listen","literacy.print_concepts.first-word","literal_action","literal_who_what","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l1.C.short_i.v9","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.A.short_a.v1","lp3.hfw_1_25.l1.C.a.v3","lp3.hfw_1_25.l1.C.i.v3","lp3.hfw_1_25.l1.C.of.v3","lp3.hfw_1_25.l1.C.to.v3","lp3.hfw_1_25.l1.C.you.v3","lp3.hfw_26_50.l1.C.one.v3","lp3.hfw_26_50.l1.C.use.v3","lp3.hfw_51_75.l1.C.two.v3","mara nearly recycled a plain bag because she thought it was empty. looking inside revealed the missing puppet shoes. at playtime, ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. she looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. she put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","match","may’s boots were on the porch when she ate lunch.","milo kept finishing his sister’s puzzle for her. he began showing one useful move, then handing the pieces back. at music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. he offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. she had no chance to try a piece. he showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","mira pushed a stopped toy car harder without success. looking underneath revealed a caught stone. leo kept adding water to a drooping plant, but it still wilted. checking its pot revealed a blocked hole; clearing it let water drain.","mira’s toy car stopped. pushing it harder did not help. she looked underneath, removed a caught stone, and the wheels turned.","mock-foundation-word:band","mock-foundation-word:crab","mock-foundation-word:drink","mock-foundation-word:fork","mock-foundation-word:frog","mock-foundation-word:nap","mock.depth.affix-careless","mock.v8.reading.0.bib","mock.v8.reading.0.dam","mock.v8.reading.0.fig","mock.v8.reading.0.gum","mock.v8.reading.0.hut","mock.v8.reading.0.mat","mock.v8.reading.0.nap","mock.v8.reading.0.pad","mock.v8.reading.0.pit","mock.v8.reading.0.rag","mock.v8.reading.0.zip","mock.v9.reading.word.0.cab","mouse names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","moving the vase happens before wiping the table, which happens before putting out the menus; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","nia guessed a string length and cut it too short. she measured before trying again. bo packed for camp but forgot his cup. next time he checked a list before closing his bag. both avoided repeating their mistakes.","nia guessed the string length and cut it too short. she measured a fresh piece before cutting, and the model fitted.","nia opened the curtains after moving a chair. she had moved the chair after hanging a photo.","noor drew a map but her friend could not follow it. she asked what was confusing, added clear signs, and her friend found the path.","noor forgot her promised fish-feeding job while playing. the next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. for the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. the teacher fed them. the next day noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","o_e","oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. he returned the sheet and they divided them. at games club, may kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. his group had none left. he returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","order","original_literacy_guide_v12_beginner_writing","packing her cup happens before watching the bird, which happens before zipping the bag; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","plants around a pond provide hiding places for frogs. insects near the water provide food. frogs lay eggs in the water, and their young begin life there before growing legs and leaving the pond’s edge.","quickly","r does not match the supplied first_letter evidence.","rain runs from a roof through a pipe into a tank. a screen catches leaves before they enter. on dry days, a gardener uses the stored water for plants, making use of rain that would otherwise run away.","ren chose a seat after handing out cards. handing out the cards happened after checking the clock.","ren could not lift a heavy crate alone, so he asked a helper to share its weight. tess promised to make twenty decorations in one evening but finished only two. for the next event she offered to make two, and the group divided the remaining work.","ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. he asked a helper to carry the other end. together they moved it onto the trolley.","rig","roots hold a plant upright and take in water. some also store food for later growth. these jobs happen below the ground, although their effects reach the stem and leaves.","sameWording","sand","sang","sentence_end_location","six flowering plants grew inside the greenhouse.","small pockets keep pencils away from the books in our backpack. wide shoulder straps spread the weight while we carry it. a buckle lets us shorten the straps when the bag hangs too low.","soft","sol left the magnifier in his coat, and the nature group could not find it. he returned it to its labelled shelf. hana put a game counter in a pencil tin by mistake. the next players lacked a counter until she put it back in the game box.","some seeds have light wings that carry them on the wind. others have hooks that cling to fur. birds carry seeds away inside fruit, and some seeds later reach the ground far from the plant they came from.","src/data/literacyMockBeginnerWritingV12.js","stock","stroking the cat happens before stacking the cushions, which happens before choosing a book; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","sub","tess hid a paint spill until she worried the model was ruined. she told gran and they cleaned it. arun concealed a torn costume because he felt embarrassed. after telling his teacher, he learned a stitch and mended it before the play.","tess spilled paint on her model and hid it. when she asked gran for help, they cleaned it before the paint dried.","tess switched on a lamp after looking at a map. she had closed a book before looking at the map.","the baker wiped the bench after setting the timer. the timer was set after the flour was weighed.","the borrowed book stayed in noor’s bag during the game.","the cake cooled on the wire rack after baking.","the children’s bags stayed in the lockers during the visit.","the class clapped for lou after moving the drums. before moving the drums, they had sung a song.","the dark opening in the centre of an eye","the finished banner was hung above the hall entrance.","the gardener","the group ate their apples after taking a photo. before taking the photo, they had counted the bags.","the group began a game without explaining it to a new child. she ran to the wrong end and stopped. they showed her the goal and played a slow round together before starting again.","the group decorated a cart while its loose wheel still wobbled. the cart could not carry their bags. they fixed the wheel first on the next cart, then added ribbons when it rolled properly.","the inside surface of a hand","the keeper counted the visitors after filling the trough. before filling the trough, she closed the shade.","the seeds sprouted in cups before planting outside.","the unfinished puzzle stayed on a tray overnight.","this","three children’s bikes needed repair.","three sailing boats were beside the jetty.","tom told a visitor that the hall was “over there.” the visitor chose the wrong door. tom named the blue door beside the stairs, and the visitor found the hall.","tom’s “over there” sent a visitor to the wrong door. naming the blue door beside the stairs helped. mina sent a message asking for “the thing” from the cupboard. her partner brought the wrong object until mina asked for the red measuring jug on the lower shelf.","tug","two builders pulled a bridge towards different tables and loosened a joint. they chose one place together before carrying it. during a play, two children both began announcing the next scene. they paused, agreed which scenes each would announce and restarted without speaking over each other.","two builders pulled their cardboard bridge towards different tables. a joint came loose. they stopped, chose one place together and carried the bridge there side by side.","two runners began from different lines. the nearer runner won, but nobody knew who was faster. they started again from one line and could compare their running.","two runners started from different lines, so their race did not show who was faster. they raced again from one line. bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. she used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","two seats beside the window were free.","two small birds were on the feeder.","uma filled a jug after picking a flower. before picking the flower, she had taken off her gloves.","una coloured a blank space that her friend wanted to leave white for snow. next time she asked and held the paper instead. dad moved a model to tidy the table, but its maker was still arranging it. on the next visit he asked which part of the table could be cleared.","una coloured the blank part of her friend’s drawing to help. her friend had wanted to leave it white for snow. on the next drawing una asked what was needed and held the paper instead.","v4-context-word-senses:bank","v4-context-word-senses:bark","v4-context-word-senses:match","v4-context-word-senses:seal","v4-context-word-senses:spring","v4-context-word-senses:trunk","v8-comprehension:main_idea:animal-care","v8-comprehension:main_idea:backpack","v8-comprehension:main_idea:book-swap","v8-comprehension:main_idea:bus-stop","v8-comprehension:main_idea:class-kitchen","v8-comprehension:main_idea:costume-room","v8-comprehension:sequencing:animal-park","v8-comprehension:sequencing:bakery-timer","v8-comprehension:sequencing:boat-outing","v8-comprehension:sequencing:book-corner","v8-comprehension:sequencing:cafe-tables","v8-comprehension:sequencing:camp-bag","v8-context-word-senses:chest","v8-context-word-senses:clip","v8-context-word-senses:coach","vet","waving a flag happens before tying his scarf, which happens before packing his notebook; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","way","weighing the flour happens before setting the timer, which happens before wiping the bench; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","when kim lost, she pushed the board and scattered the pieces. her friend stopped playing. kim helped set it up again and asked for another game without changing the old result.","worms make tunnels that let air and water enter soil. they pull dead leaves down and break them into smaller pieces. as worms move and feed, they mix material through the soil where roots grow.","“A roof directs rain into a storage tank.” is true but covers a different part only.","“A screen catches leaves before the tank.” is true but covers one part only.","“Adjust what you do to fit different needs.” applies to both characters’ different mistakes and repairs.","“Agree when to pass a game to the next pair.” is useful in episode 2, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 1.","“Agree when to return an umbrella you borrow.” is useful in episode 2, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 1.","“Ask a quiet newcomer whether they want to join a game.” is useful in episode 2, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 1.","“Ask before colouring an unfinished part of a drawing.” is useful in episode 1, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 2.","“Ask walkers which direction they want to go.” fits only one episode.","“Attach a new cover when a shared book cover tears.” is useful in episode 1, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 2.","“Bees carry pollen between different flowering plants.” is true but covers a different part only.","“Bees collect nectar to take to their hive.” is true but covers one part only.","“Buy a needed card before choosing extra wrapping paper.” is useful in episode 2, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 1.","“Carry loose lids when a box is too heavy for you.” is useful in episode 1, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 2.","“Check player names before announcing a score.” fits only the other episode.","“Check soil when deciding how much to water.” fits only one episode.","“Check that string fits before tying a booklet.” fits only the other episode.","“Check the drying notice before deciding a hat is lost.” is useful in episode 2, but does not cover the different problem and correction in episode 1.","“Check the soil before watering a drooping plant.” is useful in episode 1, but does n