 hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","Apple. Listen to the first sound. Which word has the same vowel sound?","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base.","Bo","Check unclear directions before choosing what to do.","Check what another person can actually see.","Choose a tool that fits the particular job.","Choose the first possible meaning of unclear directions.","Cover every working part when you decorate a model.","D-CONTEXT: I is correctly used at token 1; it is not the homophone error required by this sentence.","Decoration should leave the useful parts able to work.","Do needed earlier steps before starting later ones.","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through.","Eli","Find the cause instead of repeating a temporary fix.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it.","If one part works, every other part must work too.","Leave enough space for things to work properly.","Leave paper outside so there is more space to work.","Locate the digraph after earlier spoken phonemes while completing the conventional spelling of an exact supplied word.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans.","Mina","One spoken explanation is always enough to copy every part.","One successful check does not check every part.","Picture for web","Please shut the door