 confused.","A goat","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it.","A hat was necessary for a child to join the walk.","A metal clip held the two sheets together so they did not blow away. On her tablet, Mina played a short clip that showed a bird taking off, then stopped after a few seconds.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table.","A mouse nibbles a seed.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round.","A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A roof grows leaves inside a tank.","A roof keeps rain from entering a house.","A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","A seal swam past the boat and dived under the water. Back home, Kit broke the seal around the jar’s lid before opening it.","A shadow changes the shape of a toy.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","A tank makes rain above the garden.","A torch is made from several spare parts.","A toy makes light by hiding a torch.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Acts on the original guess even though the soil is already wet.","Acts on the untested guess and risks discarding the puppet shoes.","Adds a load before correcting the fault that prevents the cart carrying it.","Adds speed without settling the disagreement about where the bridge should go.","After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","After running, I could feel my heart beating inside my chest. I sat beside a wooden chest with a hinged lid and blankets inside.","Afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","Agree on a plan before working together. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Agree on a plan before working together. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Amina carrying her old clothes","An elephant has a long trunk.","Ana shared her lunch with someone who had forgotten theirs.","Anyone in the show wearing a blue ribbon was a dancer, not a singer.","Apply the named word or grammar relationship to one complete familiar context.","Arlo","Arrange three complete sentences by their prerequisite event relationships.","Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","Arun touched the rough bark covering the tree’s trunk.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading.","At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","At the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls.","At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","At the named occurrence, chest means a storage box with a lid.","At the named occurrence, clip means a small fastener that holds things together.","At the named occurrence, coach means a person who trains a team.","At the queried occurrence, \"bank\" means the edge of a river.","At the queried occurrence, \"bark\" means a tree’s outer covering.","At the queried occurrence, \"match\" means a contest between players.","At the queried occurrence, \"seal\" means a closure that keeps a lid shut.","At the queried occurrence, \"spring\" means a curled piece of metal.","At the queried occurrence, \"trunk\" means the main stem of a tree.","At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","Ava tore the cover of a shared book. She helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it.","Avoids the activity instead of correcting the misplaced tool that caused the problem.","Bea could not lift a large box, s