mock/capacity/foundation-test.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=13","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=16","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=21","/images/assessment/objective-words/cone.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/crown.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/house.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/et/wet-02.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/bin.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/red.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/trip.webp","309dfa4dc767a8e57db70f97ffa4e78d5a90ca93ba1d30ea09085ddadc3c344f","46b80555ee9ad301776499921d2dc38254c370527136070770b976a4f7f0642a","A bee drinks nectar from flowers. It carries nectar back to its hive.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden. Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil. Classes open the gate when their visit begins.","A compost heap contains leaves and fruit peel. Tiny living things break these scraps into compost.","A crane stood on long legs in the pond, spreading its wings before it flew away.","A duck spreads oil over its feathers. Water rolls off the oiled feathers.","A fish splashed.","A fish with silver scales.","A fish","A frog rests among pond plants. The plants give it places to hide.","A little bird sat on my hand.","A long piece of rope.","A pan","A rectangular floor mat","A tall palm had a ringed trunk and long leaves above the beach.","A torch shines towards a toy. The toy blocks some light and makes a shadow.","A visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge. She had left her bag before pinning on the badge. At the end, the visitor took off the badge.","Ada fixed the tear before the play began.","After","Alex, the person viewing Nina’s pictures","Along the rope.","Amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. Ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. The gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. Ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","An owl rests in a tree during the day. It hunts when it is dark.","Arun moved the screen after naming the puppet. He had opened a bag before naming it. At the end, Arun closed the bag.","Arun moved the screen after naming the puppet. He had opened a bag before naming it.","Arun opened a bag, named the puppet, then moved the screen.","At the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. Families check it before going upstairs. A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","Auntie Vee","BO","Bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. She had washed a brush before drawing the line. At the end, Bea put away the brush.","Bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. She had washed a brush before drawing the line.","Bea filled the jug after folding the napkins. She had chosen the dish before folding the napkins. At the end, Bea emptied the jug.","Bea forgot which seeds she had sown and labelled the next pots. Dad forgot which screw fitted a shelf after taking it apart. He marked the parts of the next shelf before removing them. Their notes preserved information they had previously lost.","Bea washed a brush, drew a line, then fetched some paper.","Before choosing a book, Noor stacked the cushions. She had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions. At the end, Noor put the book away.","Before choosing a book, Noor stacked the cushions. She had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","Before choosing a pear, Lina lifted her basket. She had counted her coins before lifting the basket. At the end, Lina paid for the pear.","Before packing his notebook, Arun tied his scarf. Before tying his scarf, he waved a flag. At the end, Arun folded the flag.","Before packing his notebook, Arun tied his scarf. Before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","Before putting on his hat, Eli sharpened his pencil. Before sharpening the pencil, he had counted the butterflies. At the end, Eli drew a butterfly.","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base. Kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. Counters fell through. He tried a plain tub with solid sides. The counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","Ben has a Dog.","Beside the basket full of apples.","Both groups finished their pictures without arguing.","Can","Carmen","Check independent decoding of a real short-to-long word pair without a supplied spoken answer as a separate task.","Check independent decoding, completion or construction of words with this pattern as a separate task.","Check that the pages show the whole walking route.","Children could enter only after an adult opened the gate.","Choose a map large enough for the group to share.","Choose card colors that stand out against the wall.","Choose colors that make a toy cart easy to find.","Choose flag colors that visitors can see clearly.","Choose wrapping that is large enough for the box.","Closing the drawer happened after checking the address. Before checking the address, Bo had sorted the cards. At the end, Bo put stamps on the cards.","Compare one final spoken phoneme with a spoken answer word and visible print support. sh/th/ng and ll each represent one final sound, so their spelling length does not raise the spoken comparison demand.","Complete the conventional spelling of one final spoken phoneme. sh/th/ng and doubled ll are one sound, not two.","Confuses the explicitly stated count three with the nearby count four.","Confuses the explicitly stated count two with the nearby count one.","D-CONTEXT: my is correctly used at token 3; it is not the homophone error required by this sentence.","D-CONTEXT: the is correctly used at token 3; it is not the homophone error required by this sentence.","D-OPPOSITE","D-VOWEL: this word has a different vowel sound.","DRESS","Dad counted the cups after closing a basket. He had unfolded a blanket before closing the basket. At the end, Dad folded the blanket.","Dad counted the cups after closing a basket. He had unfolded a blanket before closing the basket.","Dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat. He hung his coat after reading his ticket. At the end, Dad put away his bottle.","Dad served the soup after it was cooked.","Dad unfolded a blanket, closed a basket, then counted the cups.","Do you want some milk?","Drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat. Before putting on the coat, May had chosen a chair. At the end, May put away the chair.","E","ER","EY","Each child planted two seeds, and no child planted any more.","Each pupil carried a schoolbook into the classroom and sat down for a lesson.","Effie''s cousin","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through. Rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. Several streets were missing. She copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. Her new drawing included the streets.","Eve put out the menus after wiping the table. She had moved the vase before wiping the table. At the end, Eve collected the menus.","Eve put out the menus after wiping the table. She had moved the vase before wiping the table.","Everyone in the show was either a dancer or a singer. Every dancer wore a blue ribbon. No singer wore a blue ribbon.","Existing approved pictures identify exact spoken choices; hidden spellings preserve the sound comparison.","Four story books stood on the top shelf beside six nature books. Five more story books stood on the bottom shelf. The librarian marked each group with a label.","Give the cart a handle that is comfortable to hold.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it. Dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. The drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. Dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. The drummer could use the pedal.","Grandad tuned the violin before the concert.","He loosened the knot.","Helpers rinse empty food tubs before our model workshop. Sticky food is removed so the tubs are ready to handle. They sort clean tubs, lids and cardboard into separate trays for the builders to choose from.","Her clothes might get dirty.","How a helper replaces worn strings after instruments return.","How a high tap leaves room for a bottle.","How a repair sheet tells a team about faults.","How a station helps fill bottles and drain spills.","How a tray drains water instead of letting it collect.","How a worker tests swings before the playground opens.","How an order list helps a helper find missing supplies.","How checks find faults and arrange playground repairs.","How desk staff explain a change of platform.","How drivers pack parcels into a delivery van.","How helpers sort deliveries and check missing supplies.","How instrument loans are recorded and equipment maintained.","How labelled trolleys take books to their shelves.","How labelled tubs separate parcels for different classrooms.","How learners choose songs for a concert.","How returned books are checked in and sorted.","How scanning a returned book clears its loan.","How signs above stairs show the platform numbers.","How signs and staff help travellers find their trains.","How the teacher records names beside borrowed instruments.","How to choose games for the playground.","How to wash bottles before filling them.","How workers build a new train platform.","How writers choose names for their books.","I can bend my elbow.","I can bend my leg.","I can brush my hair.","I can eat some bread.","I can eat some meat.","I can eat some watermelon.","I can hear the rain.","I can hold the brush.","I can open the window.","I can see a zebra.","I can sweep with the broom.","I can take a photo with the camera.","I can turn on the lamp.","I can wash at the sink.","I can wave my hand.","I can wear my watch.","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again. Felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. Almost no sound came out. He moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. He could hear the trumpet again.","Jin fed the rabbit after lunch but before the music lesson.","Jo counted the shells once, but her total was wrong. She had not counted them again.","Jo tied her shoe after checking the score. She had carried the hoop before checking the score. At the end, Jo put away the hoop.","Kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. He had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket. At the end, Kai folded the blanket.","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle. Lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. Paint covered the wall around each window. She changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","Keep a record of how many beads you collect.","Keep cleaning cloths away from the toy collection.","Keep different paint colors in their own pots.","Keep loose card pieces in a labelled storage tray.","Kit put on a hat after tying a rope. Before tying the rope, Kit had waved to Gran. At the end, Kit took off the hat.","Kit put on a hat after tying a rope. Before tying the rope, Kit had waved to Gran.","Kit waved to Gran, tied a rope, then put on a hat.","Kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. Watching the bird happened after she packed her cup. At the end, Kit unpacked her cup.","Kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. Watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","Lamps light the path from the car park to our evening event. Visitors can see uneven ground beneath their feet. At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","Lia emptied her bottle after a drink, then filled it a second time. She stopped exactly at the marked line, which showed the required amount.","Luca kept dry seeds in a jar. He sowed them in cups by the window, where the first shoots appeared. Later he moved the young plants into the garden.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans. Esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. The zipper could not close. She moved some costumes into a second bag. Both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","Mara began the puzzle on the table. At bedtime she slid it onto a tray and put the tray under the sofa. The empty box stayed on the table until she finished the puzzle the next day.","Match a gift to the interests of its owner.","Match a supplied spoken word to its printed form. Changing which short or long word is spoken does not establish a harder operation.","May wore her boots along the muddy path. She left them on the porch, then ate lunch in the kitchen in her socks. The boots stayed where she had taken them off.","Maya''s brother","Measure a cupboard before choosing what to store.","Mina painted every flag except the yellow flag. She left that flag plain.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again. Owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. Water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. He poured a little water into the next jug first. That jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","Mira","Mira’s brother","Mum stitched a cloth patch over the hole in my trousers.","My brother counted the spare buttons.","My socks are in the box.","Near the fish.","Neither the red bag nor the blue bag held a towel. Each towel was in the basket.","Nia hung a photo, moved a chair, then opened the curtains.","Nia opened the curtains after moving a chair. She had moved the chair after hanging a photo. At the end, Nia took down a photo.","Nia opened the curtains after moving a chair. She had moved the chair after hanging a photo.","Noor borrowed a book from the library and put it in her bag. She left the bag in the changing room while she played on the court. The book stayed inside the bag until she went home.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon. Leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. While he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. For the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","Noor’s friend could not follow her map. Noor asked which marks were confusing and changed them. Ben’s instructions confused his team. He asked them to show where they got lost, then rewrote that part. Both used another person’s response to improve their work.","OW","One red fish swam away.","Only children wearing hats could join the walk. Amir wore a hat and joined.","Our bus beside the school.","Our bus sat in a traffic jam, with vehicles blocking the road ahead.","Our paper roof sagged under the first coin.","Our picnic cart has deep sides to stop baskets slipping off. Straps hold the drinks upright while it moves. Its large wheels roll over the bumpy grass between the gate and our picnic spot.","Our","Picture for cake","Picture for drum","Picture for flag","Picture for frog","Picture for gate","Picture for key","Picture for lid","Picture for rock","Picture for sock","Picture for tent","Picture for tie","Picture for tiger","Picture for van","Picture for vase","Picture for wig","Picture for zebra","Picture maps at the welcome desk show the rooms in our school. Visitors can follow the marked route to a classroom. Helpers also answer questions about lessons and clubs that are not shown on the maps.","Put your coat on the hook.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat. Hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. Foam spilled over the edge. For the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","Rafi slid the note beneath the door.","Rain runs from a roof into a tank. The tank keeps the water for later use.","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them. Mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. The words ran down the paper. She made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. Rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","Recognise the same in-band spoken HFW while rejecting two close real-word neighbours (one_letter_substitution, one_letter_insertion); distinguishing letters and their positions are required. The target stock, three-choice operation and silent print access are unchanged.","Reject three real neighbours that retain nk by reading the other phonemes. Matching the blend alone could distinguish the entry options but cannot answer this item.","Ren checked the clock, handed out cards, then chose a seat.","Ren chose a seat after handing out cards. Handing out the cards happened after checking the clock. At the end, Ren put away the cards.","Ren chose a seat after handing out cards. Handing out the cards happened after checking the clock.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily. Theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. Before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. He followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","Retain the other phonemes while performing exactly one add phoneme operation.","Rock was piled beside the new path, with small stones ready for the builders.","Roots take water from the soil. The water moves up into the plant.","STRUT","Sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. His cousin arrived on the wrong morning. Sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic. Pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. Her group cut strips too short for the roof. She checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. The new strips reached across.","Sam watered the plants while Jo was away.","Sam''s pencil","Say pin. Add the first sound in sock at the beginning. What word do you make?","Seven flags lined the path to the hall.","She squeezed the lemons.","She tiptoed past the dog.","Six evening tickets were set aside for the cast. Three afternoon tickets were still for sale at the same desk. Four evening tickets were left for sale.","Six flowering plants grew inside the greenhouse beside four plants with only leaves. Three more flowering plants stood outside in the sun.","Some seeds float away on the wind. Their light parts help them travel.","Sort differently colored beads into separate groups.","Spare batteries waited inside the drawer.","Substitutes a for the medial short e spelling in bench.","Substitutes a for the medial short i spelling in fin.","Substitutes a for the medial short i spelling in lid.","Substitutes a for the medial short i spelling in list.","Substitutes a for the medial short o spelling in fox.","Substitutes a for the medial short o spelling in pond.","Substitutes a for the medial short u spelling in rug.","Substitutes e for the medial short a spelling in band.","Substitutes e for the medial short a spelling in camp.","Substitutes e for the medial short a spelling in crab.","Substitutes e for the medial short a spelling in flap.","Substitutes e for the medial short i spelling in fin.","Substitutes e for the medial short i spelling in lid.","Substitutes e for the medial short i spelling in list.","Substitutes e for the medial short o spelling in fox.","Substitutes e for the medial short o spelling in pond.","Substitutes e for the medial short u spelling in rug.","Substitutes i for the medial short a spelling in band.","Substitutes i for the medial short a spelling in camp.","Substitutes i for the medial short a spelling in crab.","Substitutes i for the medial short a spelling in flap.","Substitutes i for the medial short e spelling in bench.","Sunlight reached the books on our table.","Supply the initial digraph in an exact supplied word. Another word length or later taught digraph is not a higher response operation.","Suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. When she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. She added it, then compared the two flags once more. Dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. He looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. He added that support before trying the bridge.","Tess closed a book, looked at a map, then switched on a lamp.","Tess switched on a lamp after looking at a map. She had closed a book before looking at the map. At the end, Tess opened another book.","Tess switched on a lamp after looking at a map. She had closed a book before looking at the map.","The actors stopped the fan after moving the screen. Moving the screen happened after they took a bow. At the end, the actors started the fan.","The apples in the basket.","The baker sprinkled seeds over the loaf.","The baker wiped the bench after setting the timer. The timer was set after the flour was weighed. At the end, the baker put away the flour.","The baker wiped the bench after setting the timer. The timer was set after the flour was weighed.","The basket full of apples fell over.","The basket full of fresh apples.","The bell above the door.","The cake baked in the oven. Sal moved it onto a wire rack to cool while she cleared the table. Once it was cool, she carried it to the table for tea.","The caterpillar is on a leaf.","The children entered through the garden. Their bags stayed in the lockers while the children visited the dinosaur room. They collected the bags before eating in the garden.","The clasp held Sara’s necklace closed. Sara opened the clasp and separated the two ends. She left the ends apart.","The class clapped for Lou after moving the drums. Before moving the drums, they had sung a song. At the end, the class put away the drums.","The class clapped for Lou after moving the drums. Before moving the drums, they had sung a song.","The class lifted the magnet after folding the cloth. Before folding the cloth, they had drawn a line. At the end, the class rubbed out the line.","The class sang a song, moved the drums, then clapped for Lou.","The clear sheet had no colour. It was not tinted red, blue or any other colour.","The corn is yellow.","The cyclist folded the rag after rolling in the bike. Before rolling in the bike, he had hung up his helmet. At the end, the cyclist put on his helmet.","The date on the invitation was the day of our party.","The dolphin can jump.","The edge was covered in soft foam. It could not hurt a child who bumped it, and the edge itself was not damaged.","The fan beside the desk spun its blades and blew air across the warm room.","The fish in the pond.","The group ate their apples after taking a photo. Before taking the photo, they had counted the bags. At the end, the group put away the bags.","The group ate their apples after taking a photo. Before taking the photo, they had counted the bags.","The group counted the bags, took a photo, then ate their apples.","The heavy rain.","The helpers painted the banner on the playground floor. When it dried, they hung it above the hall entrance. Paper flags stayed beneath the walkway.","The juice leaked until Mina twisted the cap tightly onto the bottle.","The kangaroo can hop.","The keeper counted the visitors after filling the trough. Before filling the trough, she closed the shade. At the end, the keeper opened the animal gate.","The keeper counted the visitors after filling the trough. Before filling the trough, she closed the shade.","The key preserves the passage''s before after relationship.","The letter arrived in an envelope with news from Gran.","The library van carries books on shelves with bars across the front. The bars hold the books in place during travel. Every week the van stops at villages where readers cannot easily reach the town library.","The lion is asleep.","The lunchbox has separate spaces for fruit and sandwiches. These stop soft food being squashed against the apples. Two clips hold the lid shut when the lunchbox tips inside a school bag.","The nurse moved the blanket after weighing the puppy. She had written the card before weighing the puppy. At the end, the nurse fed the puppy.","The penguin can swim.","The players stayed inside unless the rain stopped. The rain continued all afternoon.","The plug had joined the lamp to the socket. An adult pulled it out and left it lying on the table. Nobody put it back.","The post arrived in a bag of letters that the carrier left at our door.","The potter covered the clay after smoothing the bowl. Smoothing the bowl happened after washing her hands. At the end, the potter dried the clay.","The puppy under the chair.","The rain over the garden.","The rain stopped.","The ridged roof held several coins without sagging.","The room grew too dark for reading.","The rope across the stream.","The rope snapped.","The shark is in the water.","The snail is on a leaf.","The snake is on a rock.","The snow is cold.","The soup is hot.","The spoken word band has the short a vowel, conventionally spelled a here.","The spoken word bench has the short e vowel, conventionally spelled e here.","The spoken word camp has the short a vowel, conventionally spelled a here.","The spoken word crab has the short a vowel, conventionally spelled a here.","The spoken word fin has the short i vowel, conventionally spelled i here.","The spoken word flap has the short a vowel, conventionally spelled a here.","The spoken word fox has the short o vowel, conventionally spelled o here.","The spoken word lid has the short i vowel, conventionally spelled i here.","The spoken word list has the short i vowel, conventionally spelled i here.","The spoken word names bath.","The spoken word names butterfly.","The spoken word names chin.","The spoken word names cloud.","The spoken word names corn.","The spoken word names dolphin.","The spoken word names hair.","The spoken word names monkey.","The spoken word names mouth.","The spoken word names phone.","The spoken word names rain.","The spoken word names rice.","The spoken word names ring.","The spoken word names sink.","The spoken word names snail.","The spoken word names spider.","The spoken word names tooth.","The spoken word names watch.","The spoken word names watermelon.","The spoken word names zebra.","The spoken word pond has the short o vowel, conventionally spelled o here.","The spoken word rug has the short u vowel, conventionally spelled u here.","The teacher hung up the keys after ringing the buzzer. She had fetched the register before ringing the buzzer. At the end, the teacher opened the register.","The tiger can run.","The waiting children beside the gate.","The wet umbrella stood inside a tall vase.","The whale is in the sea.","The wheel stayed straight when we tried the cart again.","The wheel wobbled each time the cart moved.","There were two tables of lanterns. No lantern on the left table was lit. All the lanterns on the right table were lit.","This existing oral task uses replayable spoken alternatives with hidden spellings. Exact atomic phoneme clips are used for blending; whole-word sound anchors are used for changes.","This is my chin.","This task matches a supplied spoken word to its printed form. Switching the recording from a long-vowel word to a short-vowel word does not by itself establish a harder response operation.","This task selects one conventional r-controlled spelling for a heard word. Adding consonants or rarer vocabulary would not by itself increase the demand of selecting that spelling pattern.","Three children’s bikes needed repair, while five children’s bikes were ready to ride. Two adults’ bikes also needed repair and stood beside the same workbench.","Three red pencils still had blunt tips. Four blue pencils were sharpened too. Five red pencils were sharpened, and each group went into a separate pot.","Three sailing boats were tied beside the jetty with two rowing boats. Four other sailing boats lay farther out in the bay. None moved while the harbour worker counted them.","Three seats near the door were also free. Four other window seats had coats on them. Two seats beside the window were free, so the group had to choose where to sit.","Three swimmers wore green caps.","Tickets for our play show the row and seat for each visitor. Helpers use the tickets to guide families into place. A printed programme names the characters and lists the scenes so families can follow the play.","Two groups needed the same paintbrushes at once.","Two small birds perched on the feeder with one large bird. Four small birds waited on the fence. The watcher wrote down where each group was sitting.","Two used cups were on the tray, waiting to be washed. Five clean cups were on the tray. Four clean cups remained in the cupboard.","Uma filled a jug after picking a flower. Before picking the flower, she had taken off her gloves. At the end, Uma put on her gloves.","Uma filled a jug after picking a flower. Before picking the flower, she had taken off her gloves.","Uma took off her gloves, picked a flower, then filled a jug.","Umbrella. Listen to the first sound. Which word has the same vowel sound?","Under the dark cloud.","Until the heavy garden gate finally opened for all of us.","Until the soil dried, Rosa did not water the pot. She watered it as soon as it was dry.","Until we could go through the gate.","We agreed on a turn for each group.","We can play after lunch.","We folded ridges into a new piece of paper.","We found a loose nut and tightened it.","We pulled back the thick curtains.","Where is my teddy bear?","Which letters spell the vowel sound in the word you hear?","Which vowel pattern completes the word?","Which word has the long a sound?","Worms make tunnels in soil. Air can enter through these tunnels.","___ birds cannot fly.","___ close the lid.","___ lunch we rest.","___ you find my sock?","a ball used in a game","a clap made with two hands","a feather from a bird","a footprint left in sand","a handle for carrying a bottle","a hole made in a board","a line marking a playing field","a necklace worn for a party","a picture on an envelope","a pocket sewn onto some trousers","a printed address on an envelope","a ring around a bottle’s base","a set of goalposts for a game","a small band worn on a wrist","a sticker","a tear made in cloth","a wobbly table","a wooden handle on a hammer","aDa","aVa","ad