eside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. she added it, then compared the two flags once more.","switching on the torch occurs after the other two events; mention order is not event order.","t changes the first phoneme of flag.","t does not match the supplied last_letter evidence.","t is the first printed letter in turtle.","t is the last printed letter in bucket.","tag differs from tap at the final letter.","tap matches the complete spoken target. tip and top keep the consonant sounds but change the vowel.","tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. he could not remember which ones he had checked. he placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. he found the stamp in a new drawer. mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. she kept returning to shelves she had already searched. she began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. on the next shelf she found the book.","team","tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. their leaves overlapped and bent. she moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. the leaves no longer pressed against one another. arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. two pictures stuck together. he moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. they dried without sticking.","testing the microphone happens before closing the window, which happens before setting out the chairs; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","thanks names a related action, property or idea, but does not reverse the meaning of yes.","thanks","the apple is red.","the apples rolled","the baby cried","the baker lent her rolling pin to the cook.","the baker sprinkled seeds over the loaf.","the basket fell","the bench still had wet paint, so a sign warned people against sitting there.","the birds sang","the birds woke","the box is not heavy.","the boy loosened the knot and opened his parcel.","the bucket dropped","the bus stopped","the bus will come soon.","the caretaker opened the side gate.","the caretaker","the cat hid","the cat slept","the cheese tastes salty.","the child fetched a cloth","the child made a bed","the children gave their teacher some flowers, and she placed them beside the classroom window.","the children got off","the children played","the choir practices in the hall every tuesday.","the clasp held sara’s necklace closed. sara opened the clasp and separated the two ends. she left the ends apart.","the class drew the labels after opening the packet. before opening the packet, they had counted the pots.","the clear sheet had no colour. it was not tinted red, blue or any other colour.","the clock stopped","the coach showed our team how to pass the ball and planned our practice","the cookie has chocolate chips.","the date on the invitation was the day of our party. for the snack, gran cut a soft, sweet brown date in half and removed its hard stone.","the date on the invitation was the day of our party.","the dentist gave milo a sticker for sitting calmly.","the diver carried a camera beneath the water.","the doorbell rang we opened the door","the edge was covered in soft foam. it could not hurt a child who bumped it, and the edge itself was not damaged.","the empty flowerpot stood near the gate.","the fallen apple rolled down the hill.","the fan beside the desk spun its blades and blew air across the room. a football fan stood nearby, cheering for her team on the television.","the fan beside the desk spun its blades and blew air across the warm room.","the farmer got up","the fish swims in water.","the flower opened","the fox ran","the frog hid under the largest pond leaf.","the gardener brought water","the gate had been locked. dad turned the key and it could open.","the gate opened","the glue had dried our model was ready","the goalkeeper tipped the ball above the goal.","the group drank water after colouring the picture. they had crossed the bridge before colouring the picture.","the group found the tape after clipping up the plan. they had measured the card before clipping up the plan.","the hungry gull followed the fishing boat until it sailed away from the harbour.","the ice melted","the juice leaked until mina twisted the cap tightly onto the bottle.","the keeper fed the hungry penguins, so they were full before the first visitors arrived.","the keeper set the injured bird free after it healed.","the kettle boiled dad made tea","the kitten was found inside the tall cupboard.","the lamp broke","the letter arrived in an envelope with news from gran.","the librarian repaired the torn poster.","the librarian stamped the return date inside my borrowed book.","the lid was stuck. i pulled hard. at last it opened.","the lift was already full of passengers, so mei waited downstairs for the next one.","the light turned green the cars moved forward","the mouse squeaked","the new pupil new the answer to the question.","the office records where and when each lost object was found. a label stays with the object. people looking for something describe it, and the office checks the description against the label before returning it.","the one team that trained hard one the race.","the paint dried","the painted mask rested behind the curtain.","the path dried","the path flooded","the players closed the box after moving the screen. they had moved the screen after sewing the puppet’s hat.","the players ran onto the grassy pitch and placed the ball between the goals. in the music room, the singer changed the pitch of a note, first making it high and then low.","the players stayed inside unless the rain stopped. the rain continued all afternoon.","the players stopped","the plug had joined the lamp to the socket. an adult pulled it out and left it lying on the table. nobody put it back.","the post arrived in a bag of letters that the carrier left at our door.","the puddle froze","the puppy yawned","the rabbit hopped","the rabbit twitches i