word:sink","vocabulary-word:snail","vocabulary-word:spider","vocabulary-word:tooth","vocabulary-word:watch","vocabulary-word:watermelon","vocabulary-word:zebra","washing the apples happens before tying her apron, which happens before choosing a spoon; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","watch that puddle! the path is wet.","waving to her friend","we can play after Lunch.","we can play after luncH.","we can play after lunch.","we heard thunder during breakfast.","we is a different printed word from the recording of be.","we made sandcastles on the beach.","we rest on the bench.","we saw a rainbow.","weak names a different action, feeling or property; it does not mean strong.","weighing the puppy occurs after writing the card, even though it occurs before the final event.","wet differs from web at the final letter.","whale names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","when the bell rang","when the bell rang, the class lined up","where is my teddy Bear?","where is my teddy beaR?","where is my teddy bear?","where is the puppy? is it under the bed? i can hear it breathing.","which box holds the string?","while the dog ate","while the dog ate, the cat slept","who closed the window? it is warm here.","why","wind","won","wore her boots along the muddy path","worm","wrench","write that a trip happens in october.","write that the boy named eli helped you.","write that the dog named spot slept by the fire.","write that you and your sister cleaned the cage.","write that you will visit a friend on sunday.","write that your class swims on wednesday.","write that your cousin lives in madrid.","writing-capacity:complete-entry-bell","writing-capacity:complete-entry-bus","writing-capacity:edit-cap-1","writing-capacity:exclaim-detail-1","writing-capacity:exclaim-detail-2","wrote","yak spells a different word from the pictured fin.","yak spells a different word from the pictured fog.","yes and no name opposite meanings.","yet","z does not match the supplied first_letter evidence.","zap does not match the supplied read_complete_cvc_word evidence.","zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. the cardboard began to bend. she stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap. hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. the knot grew tighter. he loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. the ribbon came free without another hard pull.","zebra changes the requested initial phoneme.","ɛ","“A roof grows leaves inside a tank.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“A shadow changes the shape of a toy.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“A tank makes rain above the garden.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“A toy makes light by hiding a torch.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Bees carry hive walls out to flowers.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Ben” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Birds make seeds inside their wings.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Check bookshelves one at a time from one end.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Mark drawers that have already been searched for a stamp. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check every model bus wheel before calling it ready.” explains episode 1, but episode 2 instead concerns this different action: Test each carrying handle before lifting the box. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check that a block base is firm and level.” does not explain this correction. The spoken block description was hard to retain and a drawn plan supplied a continuing reference; stability and fair shares were not the copying problem.","“Check whether a bright growing place should be indoors.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Find out which door a collector actually means. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Choose a blanket large enough for the visitors.” does not explain this correction. The friend waited at the old place because the move had not been explained; blanket size and carrying food would not tell the friend where to go.","“Choose a box that is easy to carry.” does not explain this correction. The parcel reached the wrong door because the direction was unclear; box size and keeping a path clear would not identify the intended door.","“Choose a bus color that passengers can recognize.” does not explain this correction. An unchecked wheel stuck after one different wheel had passed a check; bus color and seat space would not test the other wheels.","“Choose a puzzle with enough pieces for everyone.” does not explain this correction. Pushing bent the puzzle piece, while turning it revealed the fit; sorting colors or sharing pieces would not change the failing method.","“Choose clear pictures of the objects to collect.” does not explain this correction. The younger children could not see past the shelf; strong paper and clear pictures would not move the list into their view.","“Choose paint colors that show against the background.” does not explain this correction. The paint dried while Alma searched for tools; color contrast and protecting a finished picture would not have put the tools ready beforehand.","“Choose plant labels that can survive getting wet.” does not explain this correction. The seedlings pressed against one another because they were crowded; labels and counting would not leave room between the leaves.","“Choose plants that fit the space on a shelf.” does not explain this correction. The same puddle returned because the tray was cracked; plant size and dividing watering jobs would not repair the leak.","“Choose scissors suited to the thickness of the paper.” does not explain this correction. Cutting the only pattern removed the earlier version; suitable 