ole walking route.” does not explain this correction. The wind scattered loose pages, and moving indoors sheltered them; map size and route coverage would not stop the gust.","“Choose a map large enough for the group to share.” does not explain this correction. The wind scattered loose pages, and moving indoors sheltered them; map size and route coverage would not stop the gust.","“Choose a picnic place with room for everyone.” does not explain this correction. The note left out the day, causing an arrival on the wrong morning; an envelope or larger picnic site would not supply the missing day.","“Choose card colors that stand out against the wall.” does not explain this correction. Excess glue soaked and wrinkled the card; the card colors and the storage tray would not reduce that excess.","“Choose colors that make a toy cart easy to find.” does not explain this correction. Wrapping jammed a moving wheel; attractive colors and a comfortable handle would not clear the wheel.","“Choose colors that make the model’s shape easy to see.” does not explain this correction. The attractive thin base bent under the load; visible colors and display measurements would not make that base stiff enough.","“Choose fabric that will move freely in the wind.” does not explain this correction. Comparison revealed a missing stripe after Suri thought she had finished; fabric movement and the display pole would not reveal that omission.","“Choose flag colors that visitors can see clearly.” does not explain this correction. The flag paint cracked because it had not been tried on spare paper; separating colors or making flags visible would not test that paint.","“Choose strong paper for a pocket that holds books.” does not explain this correction. The pocket was too narrow for the actual book; strong paper and an owner name would not establish the required size.","“Choose wrapping that is large enough for the box.” does not explain this correction. The empty box had been tied before the gift was inside, so the ribbon had to be undone; wrapping size and gift choice would not correct that order.","“Dad” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Eli” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Give every player a chance to lead the music.” does not explain this correction. Eli lost his place in a long pattern and succeeded after practicing its short parts; choosing an instrument or sharing leadership was not the difficulty.","“Give the cart a handle that is comfortable to hold.” does not explain this correction. Wrapping jammed a moving wheel; attractive colors and a comfortable handle would not clear the wheel.","“Hana” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Hang a wet coat where it can dry.” does not explain this correction. A similar appearance led Amir to take another coat; drying coats or lowering hooks would not identify the owner.","“Keep a note of who has borrowed each tray.” does not explain this correction. Beans spilled because the small tray was overfilled; sorting beans and recording tray loans would not provide more space.","“Keep a record of how many beads you collect.” does not explain this correction. The wide cup could not direct beads into the narrow neck; sorting or counting beads would not change that opening.","“Keep cleaning cloths away from the toy collection.” does not explain this correction. Ren could not restore the shelves to their places and solved this with matching marks; choosing cupboard contents or moving cloths would not record the arrangement.","“Keep coats low enough for children to reach.” does not explain this correction. A similar appearance led Amir to take another coat; drying coats or lowering hooks would not identify the owner.","“Keep different paint colors in their own pots.” does not explain this correction. The flag paint cracked because it had not been tried on spare paper; separating colors or making flags visible would not test that paint.","“Keep loose card pieces in a labelled storage tray.” does not explain this correction. Excess glue soaked and wrinkled the card; the card colors and the storage tray would not reduce that excess.","“Listen to other players before choosing an instrument.” does not explain this correction. Eli lost his place in a long pattern and succeeded after practicing its short parts; choosing an instrument or sharing leadership was not the difficulty.","“Match a gift to the interests of its owner.” does not explain this correction. The empty box had been tied before the gift was inside, so the ribbon had to be undone; wrapping size and gift choice would not correct that order.","“Measure a cupboard before choosing what to store.” does not explain this correction. Ren could not restore the shelves to their places and solved this with matching marks; choosing cupboard contents or moving cloths would not record the arrangement.","“Measure the model before deciding where to display it.” does not explain this correction. The attractive thin base bent under the load; visible colors and display measurements would not make that base stiff enough.","“Mira’s brother” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Mira” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Send a picnic invitation in a strong envelope.” does not explain this correction. The note left out the day, causing an arrival on the wrong morning; an envelope or larger picnic site would not supply the missing day.","“Sort differently colored beads into separate groups.” does not explain this correction. The wide cup could not direct beads into the narrow neck; sorting or counting beads would not change that opening.","“Sort the beans by size before comparing them.” does not explain this correction. Beans spilled because the small tray was overfilled; sorting beans and recording tray loans would not provide more space.","“Tessa” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Use a 